## Supporting Data

### Performance Metrics for AI-Developed Features
- **Bug Resolution Time:** Reduced by 45% (March 2026 vs. January 2026)  
- **Build Times:** Reduced by 60% following coding agent integration (March 26, 2026)  
- **Feature Accuracy:** 94% accuracy in AI-developed logic optimization, pending further refinement  

### Client Feedback Highlights
- **Positive:** Faster delivery times, cost savings on development cycles  
- **Negative:** Concerns over transparency and maintainability of AI-generated code  

### Employee Sentiment Survey (Preliminary Results)
- **Participation Rate:** 68%  
- **Key Concerns:**
  - Job security (72% of respondents)
  - Ethical implications of AI-driven layoffs (63% of respondents)
  - Confidence in AI system reliability (58% of respondents)

### Risk Overview
- **Technical Risks:**
  - Recurring UI glitches in flagship SaaS product (identified March 30, 2026)  
  - Subtle flaws in coding agent’s logic optimization (identified March 29, 2026)  
- **Business Risks:**
  - Client hesitation due to perceived AI-driven reorganization  
  - Potential PR fallout from media coverage and employee protests  

---

## Action Items for HugeSmoothTech Team
1. Provide detailed documentation of AI-generated code and project deliverables for client review.
2. Assign a dedicated team to address recurring UI glitches and complete fixes by the next sprint cycle.
3. Organize follow-up meetings with the client to address any unresolved concerns.
4. Work with HR and Legal to finalize updates to the employee handbook, addressing AI policy changes.

